    'Naegele\'s rule estimates the due date by adding 9 months and 7 days to the first day of the last menstrual period (or subtracting 3 months and adding 7 days, and adding a year): 10 January + 7 days = 17 January; + 9 months = 17 October. It assumes a 28-day cycle with ovulation on day 14; for longer cycles, days are added (e.g., 7 extra days for a 35-day cycle). Pregnancy lasts about 280 days (40 weeks) from the LMP. A first-trimester crown–rump length scan is more accurate and is used to confirm or correct the date.',
